Root cause (verified by main agent):
  1. Both surfaces have allowlist middleware wired:
     - Backend  (FastAPI): services/ip_allowlist/middleware.py
     - Frontend (craco):   plugins/ip-allowlist/middleware.js
     Both read the same 4 env vars from /app/backend/.env:
       SPINE_ALLOWED_IPS · SPINE_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS ·
       OWNER_ALLOWLIST_IPS · ALLOWLIST_MODE
     (craco.config.js lines 14-32 mirrors backend .env into process.env
      at dev-server bootstrap; the mirror happens ONCE at process start.)

  2. At 2026-08-26T09:20Z strict flip, main agent ran:
       sudo supervisorctl restart backend
     but NOT:
       sudo supervisorctl restart frontend
     So the FastAPI process re-read the .env (saw ALLOWLIST_MODE=strict),
     but the craco Node process kept its pre-flip mirror in memory —
     it still had ALLOWLIST_MODE=permissive from R8 (2026-08-26T05:20Z).

  3. Original 20260826T092000Z_w10_strict_flip_verified.log exercised
     only backend probes (all against http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/...).
     No probe hit the frontend surface at http://127.0.0.1:3000/.
